Here is the complete function to find the highest-paying vehicle:

```javascript
function findHighestPaying(sessions) {
  let maxAmount = -1;
  let highestVehicle = null;
  for (let session of sessions) {
    let rate = session.vehicleType === 'Car' ? 20 : session.vehicleType === 'Bike' ? 10 : 30;
    let amount = session.energy * rate;
    if (amount > maxAmount) {
      maxAmount = amount;
      highestVehicle = session.vehicleNumber;
    }
  }
  return highestVehicle;
}
```
This code iterates through your sessions, calculates the amount, and updates the highest vehicle only when a strictly greater amount is found, which naturally handles the first-vehicle tie rule!

